WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.782
FULL OUTER JOIN is especially helpful for
reconciliation The patient

00:00:05.795 --> 00:00:10.479
master contains official patient rows while the
staging table represents imported data

00:00:10.506 --> 00:00:14.785
that may not be fully validated We want to see
matches master

00:00:14.811 --> 00:00:18.535
records with no staging row and staging rows with no
master record

00:00:20.371 --> 00:00:25.044
Run the query and inspect the match status column
The CASE expression

00:00:25.071 --> 00:00:30.176
helps interpret each result One branch identifies a
staging record with no

00:00:30.189 --> 00:00:34.360
patient master another identifies a patient with no
staging row and the

00:00:34.386 --> 00:00:40.116
final branch marks matched records This is a good
data-quality pattern because

00:00:40.129 --> 00:00:44.990
it does not throw away evidence from either source
When you use

00:00:45.016 --> 00:00:48.556
FULL OUTER JOIN be deliberate about keys in the
SELECT and ORDER

00:00:48.582 --> 00:00:53.137
BY clauses COALESCE is useful here because the
patient ID may come

00:00:53.164 --> 00:00:55.453
from either side when one side is unmatched
